{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ec7e39d99b57bc5ac7", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Kinetic Theory of Gases - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f3a"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ef5", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e8e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48da"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edc"], "question": {"text": "The pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>)</mo></math> relationship of an ideal gas obeys the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo></math> constant. The volume expansion coefficient of the gas will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "0ad0cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e8f"}, {"id": "234070", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e90"}, {"id": "e66f28", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e91"}, {"id": "e61f5e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e92"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e93", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "In a dilute gas at pressure&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;and temperature &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math>&#39;, the time between successive collision of a molecule varies with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;as :"}, "options": [{"id": "8d271e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e94"}, {"id": "eacc5f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e95"}, {"id": "544660", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e96"}, {"id": "3a02c2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e97"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e98", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c9"], "question": {"text": "<p>Which statements are correct about degrees of freedom?</p><p>A. A molecule with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> degrees of freedom has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> different ways of storing energy.</p><p>B. Each degree of freedom is associated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math> average energy per mole.</p><p>C. A monoatomic gas molecule has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> rotational degree of freedom where as diatomic molecule has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> rotational degrees of freedom</p><p>D. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> has a total to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> degrees of freedom.</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the option given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7e1935", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e99"}, {"id": "faea6b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e9a"}, {"id": "617f36", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e9b"}, {"id": "a009b0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e9c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e9d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01f"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement (I) : The mean free path of gas molecules is inversely proportional to square of molecular diameter.\nStatement (II) : Average kinetic energy of gas molecules is directly proportional to absolute temperature of gas.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "f569b0", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e9e"}, {"id": "d1b91d", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905e9f"}, {"id": "4dbfae", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea0"}, {"id": "b7a666", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["6162fb096ed13040ec84a530"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider a sample of oxygen behaving like an ideal gas. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>,&nbsp;the ratio of root-mean-square (RMS) velocity to the average velocity of the gas molecule would be :</p><p>(Molecular weight of oxygen is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e56861", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea3"}, {"id": "29a0a7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea4"}, {"id": "5c7dfe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea5"}, {"id": "5cf8c2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566a"], "question": {"text": "An unknown metal of mass <math><mn>192</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>g</mi></math> heated to a temperature of <math><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> was immersed into a brass calorimeter of mass <math><mn>128</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>g</mi></math> containing <math><mn>240</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>g</mi></math> of water at a temperature of <math><msup><mrow><mn>8.4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Calculate the specific heat of the unknown metal if water temperature stabilizes at <math><msup><mrow><mn>21.5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> <math><mo>(</mo></math> Specific heat of brass is <math><mn>394</mn><mi>J</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "898e29", "text": "<math><mn>916</mn><mi> </mi><mi>J</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea8"}, {"id": "840b7e", "text": "<math><mn>458</mn><mi> </mi><mi>J</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ea9"}, {"id": "26fba9", "text": "<math><mn>654</mn><mi> </mi><mi>J</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eaa"}, {"id": "83ffc3", "text": "<math><mn>1232</mn><mi> </mi><mi>J</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eab"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eac", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5a"], "question": {"text": "A cylindrical container of volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></math> contains one mole of hydrogen and two moles of carbon dioxide. Assume the temperature of the mixture is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The pressure of the mixture of gases is :<br />[Take gas constant as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "63f3de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ead"}, {"id": "cb3377", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>249</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eae"}, {"id": "96f168", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eaf"}, {"id": "8dbf39", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48da"], "concepts": ["60f34752eff4df09e43c25d3"], "question": {"text": "A balloon carries a total load of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>185</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> at normal pressure and temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;What load will the balloon carry on rising to a height at which the barometric pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi></math> and the temperature is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Assuming the volume constant?"}, "options": [{"id": "5d5409", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>214</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb2"}, {"id": "6c75cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>123</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb3"}, {"id": "80811f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>219</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>07</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb4"}, {"id": "b0ffcb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>181</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f06"], "question": {"text": "Match the $\\mathrm {List-I}$ with $\\mathrm {List-II}$<br/>$\\begin{array}{|l|l|l|l|}\\hline & \\text{List-I} & & \\text{List-II} \\\\ \\hline \\text{A.} & \\text{Triatomic rigid gas} & \\text{I.} & \\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{V}}}=\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\hline \\text{B.} & \\begin{array}{l} \\text{Diatomic non-rigid} \\\\ \\text{gas} \\end{array} & \\text{II.} & \\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{V}}}=\\frac{7}{5} \\\\ \\hline \\text{C.} & \\text{Monoatomic gas} & \\text{III.} & \\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{V}}}=\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\hline \\text{D.} & \\text{Diatomic rigid gas} & \\text{IV }& \\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{V}}}=\\frac{9}{7} \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}$<br/>Choose the $\\mathrm {correct}$ answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "3ce158", "text": "A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb7"}, {"id": "dc7886", "text": "A-III, B-II, C-IV, D-I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb8"}, {"id": "a094b0", "text": "A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eb9"}, {"id": "1f1cfd", "text": "A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905eba"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ebb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["6162fb086ed13040ec84a448"], "question": {"text": "A gas mixture consists of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of oxygen and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of argon at temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. Assuming the gases to be ideal and the oxygen bond to be rigid, the total internal energy (in units of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>) of the mixutre is :"}, "options": [{"id": "85c34f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ebc"}, {"id": "e3893c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ebd"}, {"id": "b63481", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ebe"}, {"id": "680a4e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ebf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ec0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c682e"], "question": {"text": "An ideal gas is enclosed in a cylinder at pressure of <math><mn>2</mn></math> atm and temperature, <math><mn>300</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The mean time between two successive collisions is <math><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi>s</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the pressure is doubled and temperature is increased to <math><mn>500</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the mean time between two successive collisions will be close to:"}, "options": [{"id": "5e32d3", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mo>x</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mi>s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ec1"}, {"id": "17dd20", "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mo>x</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi>s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905ec2"}, {"id": "944877", "text": "<math><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>x</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><