sub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> molecule would be equal to the rms speed of a nitrogen molecule, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> ).<br />&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "dafa0a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f1b"}, {"id": "71a9d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f1c"}, {"id": "d4f9c6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f1d"}, {"id": "16b73c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f1e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f1f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52af"], "question": {"text": "<p>A monoatomic gas performs a work of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>Q</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is the heat supplied to it. The molar heat capacity of the gas will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> during this transformation.</p><p>Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the gas constant.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "93b86a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f20"}, {"id": "0b173e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f21"}, {"id": "22e204", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f22"}, {"id": "7ba054", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f23"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f24", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01f"], "question": {"text": "<p>The average translational kinetic energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas molecules at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>&#8728;</mo></mmultiscripts></math> becomes equal to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>.</mo></math> of an electron accelerated from rest through a potential difference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>volt</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>38</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> (Fill the nearest integer).</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "292e02", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f25"}, {"id": "401705", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f26"}, {"id": "9d994c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f27"}, {"id": "2fd94f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f28"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f29", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566a"], "question": {"text": "A monoatomic gas of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>u</mi></math> is kept in an insulated container. The container is moving with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the container is suddenly stopped then a change in temperature of the gas (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math>gas constant)&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;Value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is,"}, "options": [{"id": "10444a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f2a"}, {"id": "683fef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f2b"}, {"id": "2a604c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f2c"}, {"id": "d823a3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f2d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f2e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["6162fb086ed13040ec84a448"], "question": {"text": "A system consists of two types of gas molecules <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> having&nbsp;the same number density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>25</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The diameter of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>A</mi></math> respectively. They suffer collisions at room temperature. The ratio of average distance covered by the molecule <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> between two successive collisions is ___________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "177c04", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f2f"}, {"id": "5d4a88", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f30"}, {"id": "229762", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f31"}, {"id": "0a694d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f32"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:28.793Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:28.793Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905f39"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:15:56.859Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:57:59.329Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "title": "Physics", "shortName": "Phy"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1e399cbf3c651303c